\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Positive Gaussian laws and covariance}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{For the [alternating four-cycle action](fdip-002P) at #{t=m=1},
the [partition function](fdip-0005) and
[opposite-vertex covariance](fdip-002Z) are
##{Z=\frac{4\pi^2}{3\sqrt5},\qquad
 \operatorname{Cov}(\phi(0),\phi(2))=\frac{2}{15}.}
The [exact cycle calculation](fdip-0037) derives both from the four
precision eigenvalues #{1,3,3,5}, using the
[counting-coordinate reference volume](fdip-003U).}

\p{More generally, a [positive quadratic action](fdip-0004) on a finite
real inner-product space has a [finite Gaussian normalizer](fdip-002T).
[Absolute polynomial moments](fdip-002W) make its expectation a
[polynomial state](fdip-002X), and the [covariance theorem](fdip-000B)
identifies inverse precision as its covariance operator. The
[conditional kernel](fdip-003A) then describes the retained
variables at a fixed eliminated value and distinguishes conditioning
from the [retained marginal](fdip-000E). Zero modes require the separate
constraints used for [massless laws](fdip-003V).}

